# Each mutation swaps a piece of ImportRun.tla for a plausible bug in the code it models and
# names the rule that must break on it. `scripts/formal --mutations` must print DETECTED for each.

# Before 2026-11-06: a copy renamed into place whose Photo row was still in the open
# transaction (up to 500 ms of them) was copied again on resume, as -2, and the first stayed.
mutation resume copies again a file whose copy is already in the folder
detects OneCopyEach on copy NoStrayCopyWhenDone on copy
-        ELSE IF Copied(i) # {}
+        ELSE IF FALSE

mutation resume skips a file whose Photo row was not yet committed
detects AllImportedWhenDone on copy
-        ELSE IF row[i] # "none" THEN i' = i + 1 /\ UNCHANGED <<copy, tmp, row, slotOf, pc>>
+        ELSE IF row[i] # "none" \/ Copied(i) # {} THEN i' = i + 1 /\ UNCHANGED <<copy, tmp, row, slotOf, pc>>

mutation the row is saved before the copy is renamed into place
detects RowHasCopy on copy
-     /\ tmp' = [tmp EXCEPT ![i] = "full"]
-     /\ pc' = "rename"
+     /\ tmp' = [tmp EXCEPT ![i] = "full"]
+     /\ row' = [row EXCEPT ![i] = "saved"]
+     /\ slotOf' = [slotOf EXCEPT ![i] = Free(i)]
+     /\ pc' = "rename"
-     /\ UNCHANGED <<copy, row, slotOf, up, i, crashes, finished>>
+     /\ UNCHANGED <<copy, up, i, crashes, finished>>

mutation the copy is copied into place, not renamed, and its temporary file stays
detects NoTmpWhenDone on copy
-     /\ tmp' = [tmp EXCEPT ![i] = "none"]
-     /\ UNCHANGED <<row, up, i, crashes, finished>>
+     /\ UNCHANGED <<tmp, row, up, i, crashes, finished>>
